            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0642" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2–146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Political Adviser in
                        Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Benninghoff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-07">February 7, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Moscow tel 310 Feb 1 follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Soviet press Feb 1 carries Tass Chungking despatch on differences,
                            within Kim Koo ‘govt’. Quotes Seoul correspondent of <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Central News</hi> that Kim Koo has admitted
                            split in his organization and confirmed report Kim Choo Si and Kim Yak
                            San have left so-called National Liberation Committee. Gives reason for
                            split as Kim Koo’s full alignment with rightist elements.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
